---
import Prose from './Prose.astro';
import CodeBlock from './CodeBlock.astro';
import {
  ROOT_TREE,
  ROOT_DIR_NOTES,
  BACKEND_SRC_TREE,
  BACKEND_DIR_NOTES,
  FEATURE_MODULE_TREE,
} from '../data/guide';

const enforceRule = `# backend/CLAUDE.md

When adding a feature, create backend/src/modules/<name>/ with:
  <name>.routes.ts
  <name>.controller.ts
  <name>.service.ts
  <name>.schema.ts     # Zod — the validation authority
  <name>.test.ts`;

const notesList = 'mt-3 grid gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm sm:grid-cols-[14rem_1fr]';
---

<Prose class="max-w-none">
  <p>
    TechCart is one npm-workspaces monorepo with a flat structure: three workspaces &mdash;
    buyer-app, admin-app and backend &mdash; sharing a single API and a single database.
  </p>

  <h3>Repository root</h3>
  <CodeBlock title="TechCart/" code={ROOT_TREE} />
  <dl class={notesList}>
    {ROOT_DIR_NOTES.map((entry) => (
      <div class="contents">
        <dt class="font-mono text-fg">{entry.path}</dt>
        <dd class="text-muted">{entry.note}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <h3>Inside the backend</h3>
  <CodeBlock title="backend/src/" code={BACKEND_SRC_TREE} />
  <dl class={notesList}>
    {BACKEND_DIR_NOTES.map((entry) => (
      <div class="contents">
        <dt class="font-mono text-fg">{entry.path}</dt>
        <dd class="text-muted">{entry.note}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <h3>The feature-module pattern</h3>
  <p>
    Every feature is a single folder under modules/ holding its route definitions, controller,
    service, Zod schema and tests together. Adding a feature means adding one folder &mdash; nothing
    is scattered across a routes tree, a controllers tree and a services tree.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock title="a feature module" code={FEATURE_MODULE_TREE} />

  <h3>Why a flat npm-workspaces monorepo</h3>
  <p>
    The structure mirrors the sibling LeafFlow project and is deliberately simpler than pnpm plus
    Turborepo. There is no shared packages directory &mdash; validation schemas live in the backend
    only &mdash; which keeps the build to exactly three workspaces.
  </p>

  <h3>Enforcing it with Claude Code</h3>
  <p>
    Structure that is not enforced drifts. TechCart keeps it honest with a scoped backend/CLAUDE.md
    that states the layout as a rule:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock title="backend/CLAUDE.md" code={enforceRule} />
  <p>Backed up by:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      an optional ESLint no-restricted-imports rule, or a hook that rejects new files outside an
      allowed path;
    </li>
    <li>a PR-checklist item &mdash; &ldquo;new code follows the feature-module layout&rdquo;.</li>
  </ul>
</Prose>
